.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY_TODATA 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY_todata ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY_export
.Nd functions to return keys as an array of key parameters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/evp.h
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_todata
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "int selection"
.Fa "OSSL_PARAM **params"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo EVP_PKEY_export
.Fa "const EVP_PKEY *pkey"
.Fa "int selection"
.Fa "OSSL_CALLBACK *export_cb"
.Fa "void *export_cbarg"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The functions described here are used to extract
.Sy EVP_PKEY
key values as an array of
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3 .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_todata
extracts values from a key
.Fa pkey
using the
.Fa selection .
.Fa selection
is described in
.Xr EVP_PKEY_fromdata 3 .
.Xr OSSL_PARAM_free 3
should be used to free the returned parameters in
.Em *params .
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_export
is similar to
.Fn EVP_PKEY_todata
but uses a callback
.Fa export_cb
that gets passed the value of
.Fa export_cbarg .
See
.Xr openssl-core.h 7
for more information about the callback.
Note that the
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
array that is passed to the callback is not persistent after the
callback returns.
The user must preserve the items of interest, or use
.Fn EVP_PKEY_todata
if persistence is required.
.Sh NOTES
These functions only work with key management methods coming from a
provider.
This is the mirror function to
.Xr EVP_PKEY_fromdata 3 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_todata
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_export
return 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3 ,
.Xr openssl-core.h 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_fromdata 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-RSA 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-EC 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-DSA 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-ED25519 7
.Xr EVP_PKEY-ED448 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-DH 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-X25519 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-X448 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-ML-DSA 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-ML-KEM 7 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY-SLH-DSA 7 .
.Sh HISTORY
These functions were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
Support for
.Sy ML-DSA ,
.Sy ML-KEM
and
.Sy SLH-DSA
was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
